---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { currentMonthYear } from '../utils/site-date';

const title = "About Us | Free Airport Parking Appeal Templates | AppealAirportPCN";
const description = "Learn about AppealAirportPCN.co.uk, a free resource providing legal templates and guides to help UK drivers appeal unfair airport drop-off charges. Strong legal grounds, easy to use.";
const canonical = "https://appealairportpcn.co.uk/about/";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  "name": "About AppealAirportPCN.co.uk",
  "description": description,
  "url": canonical,
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN.co.uk" },
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}>
  <header class="page-banner about-banner">
    <nav class="breadcrumb">
      <div class="wrap"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/about/">About</a></div>
    </nav>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>About Us</h1>
      <p class="page-banner-meta">Free Parking Appeal Resources for UK Drivers</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main>
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="blog-post about-content">
        <p>Airports charge you to drop someone off. Miss the payment and you get a PCN.</p>
        <p>I think they're unfair, and unenforceable. This site helps you challenge them. For free.</p>

        <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li>Free appeal templates for six UK airports: Heathrow, Gatwick, Stansted, Luton, Manchester and Birmingham.</li>
            <li>Plain-English guides to the rules behind them. These cover POFA, POPLA, parking signs and the consideration period.</li>
            <li>Warnings about fake payment sites that add fees.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>

        <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>These drop-offs feel designed to collect the fees. You're automatically entered into a contract that you have no way of declining when you drive in. You have a short, forgettable window to pay, and they don't provide any reminder.</p>
        <p>It's easy to drive in, and out, and forget all about it. And that's intentional.</p>
        <p>I dislike this kind of greedy, predatory behaviour. I think the charges are unfair. Dropping someone off isn't a luxury. And if you need help to dispute a charge, that help should be free.</p>
        <p>So everything here is free.</p>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Key Fact:</strong> Airport operators lose a significant percentage of appeals at POPLA (the independent adjudicator) when these legal points are properly raised.
        </div>

        <h2>How I write the guides</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every article lists its sources at the bottom. These are laws, court cases, the Single Code of Practice, and the airports' own pages.</li>
          <li>I use official sources first. Forum posts help but they're marked accordingly.</li>
          <li>I mention when something is uncertain, however the arguments I provide are not.</li>
          <li>I stay up to date with the laws and parking operators.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>For example, the BPA Code of Practice was replaced by the Single Code of Practice on 1 October 2024. I updated the guides and templates to match.</p>

        <h2>What I can't promise</h2>
        <p>Appeals don't always win. These companies will try many tricks in an attempt to get you to pay.</p>
        <p>Sometimes they may even rule against the law, hoping you won't escalate. I also have advice on what to do if they try this. Don't let them win.</p>

        <h2>What I don't do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>I don't charge for templates or advice.</li>
          <li>I don't ask for your personal details.</li>
          <li>I don't file appeals for you.</li>
          <li>I'm not a law firm, and I'm not connected to any airport or parking company. Just a passionate individual.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You should never pay a website to appeal a PCN for you. Appeals are free.</p>

        <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
        <p>Hosting costs are covered by optional donations through Ko-fi. If the site helped you, consider <a href="https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/drop-off-and-pick-up/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">donating £5</a> to help my work.</p>
        <p>My templates are provided "as is" for informational purposes. Users are responsible for ensuring the content is appropriate for their situation.</p>

        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>Have questions about the resources or found a mistake? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>. I value user feedback and continuously update the guides based on new case law and operator practices.</p>

        <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>Everything on this site is general information. It isn't legal advice. If your case is complicated, or a court claim arrives, talk to Citizens Advice or a solicitor.</p>

        <p><em>Last updated: <span data-current-month-year>{currentMonthYear}</span></em></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>